, version: string): PluginManifest | null;\n  list(): PluginManifest[];\n  search(query: string): PluginManifest[];\n  remove(name: string, version: string): boolean;\n  listVersions(name: string): string[];\n  update(name: string, version: string, updates: Partial<PluginManifest>): void;\n\nRequirements:\n- A single plugin name can have MULTIPLE registered versions. Store as a Map<string, Map<string, PluginManifest>> (name -> version -> manifest).\n- register: add/overwrite the manifest for its (name, version).\n- get(name): return the manifest for the HIGHEST/latest version of that plugin (compare versions; you may use the 'semver' package, semver.rcompare or semver.sort, which is a dependency). Return null if the plugin is not registered.\n- getVersion(name, version): exact lookup, null if missing.\n- list(): return all manifests across all names and versions (flattened array).\n- search(query): case-insensitive match of query against manifest name OR description; return matching manifests.\n- remove(name, version): delete that specific version; return true if it existed, false otherwise. Clean up the empty inner map if the last version is removed.\n- listVersions(name): return the list of version strings registered for that name (empty array if none).\n- update(name, version, updates): merge the partial updates into the existing manifest for (name, version). If it doesn't exist, do nothing (or throw — prefer no-op silently). Do not allow changing identity in a way that breaks the map key; just merge fields.\n`)\n\nconst RESOLVER = shared(`\nTASK: Create file src/resolver/index.ts implementing the Version Resolver using the 'semver' npm package.\n\nExport a factory: export function createResolver(): ResolverService\n\nResolverService interface:\n  resolve(constraints: VersionConstraint[], available: Record<string, string[]>): ResolvedVersion[];\n  satisfies(version: string, range: string): boolean;\n  maxSatisfying(versions: string[], range: string): string | null;\n  validRange(range: string): boolean;\n\nVersionConstraint = { name: string; range: string }\nResolvedVersion = { name: string; version: string; satisfies: string }  // satisfies = the range it satisfied\n\nRequirements (use 'semver'):\n- satisfies(version, range): return semver.satisfies(version, range). Guard against invalid input returning false rather than throwing.\n- maxSatisfying(versions, range): return semver.maxSatisfying(versions, range) (the highest version in the list satisfying the range), or null.\n- validRange(range): return true if semver.validRange(range) is non-null, else false.\n- resolve: for each constraint, look up available[constraint.name] (default to [] if missing), pick the maxSatisfying version for constraint.range. If a satisfying version exists, push { name, version, satisfies: constraint.range }. If none satisfies (or the range is invalid, or no versions available), SKIP that constraint (do not include it in the result). Return the array of resolved versions.\nImport: import semver from 'semver';  (verify the correct default-import form for the 'semver' package under esModuleInterop; you may instead import individual functions, e.g. import { satisfies, maxSatisfying, validRange } from 'semver';)\n`)\n\nconst RUNNER = shared(`\nTASK: Create file src/runner/index.ts implementing the Sandboxed Runner using the Node.js built-in 'vm' module (NOT vm2).\n\nExport a factory: export function createRunner(): RunnerService\n\nRunnerService interface:\n  execute(code: string, context?: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<SandboxResult>;\n  executeWithTimeout(code: string, timeoutMs: number, context?: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<SandboxResult>;\n\nSandboxResult = { success: boolean; output: unknown; duration: number; memoryUsed: number; error?: string }\n\nRequirements:\n- Use: import vm from 'node:vm'; import { performance } from 'node:perf_hooks'; (and process for memoryUsage).\n- execute(code, context): delegate to executeWithTimeout with a sensible DEFAULT timeout (e.g. 5000 ms).\n- executeWithTimeout(code, timeoutMs, context):\n  * Build a sandbox object that contains the provided context variables (spread context in). Do NOT expose require, process, or other host globals beyond what is reasonable. You MAY provide a minimal safe console that does nothing or buffers, but keep it simple.\n  * Measure duration with performance.now() before/after. duration in milliseconds (number).\n  * Measure memoryUsed as the difference in process.memoryUsage().heapUsed before/after (number of bytes; if negative, clamp to 0).\n  * Run with vm.runInNewContext(code, sandbox, { timeout: timeoutMs }). The 'output' field is the value returned/evaluated by the code (the completion value of the script).\n  * On success: { success: true, output, duration, memoryUsed }.\n  * On any thrown error or timeout: { success: false, output: undefined, duration, memoryUsed, error: <error message string> }. A vm timeout throws an error whose message mentions \"Script execution timed out\" — capture it. NEVER let the function reject; always resolve a SandboxResult.\n- The methods return Promises (async functions are fine) but execution itself is synchronous vm; that's acceptable.\n`)\n\nconst REVIEWS = shared(`\nTASK: Create file src/reviews/index.ts implementing the Review System. Use 'better-sqlite3' for persistence (an in-memory database is fine and preferred to avoid filesystem side effects).\n\nExport a factory: export function createReviews(): ReviewService\n\nReviewService interface:\n  addReview(review: Omit<Review, 'id' | 'createdAt' | 'flagged'>): Review;\n  getReviews(pluginName: string): Review[];\n  getAverageRating(pluginName: string): number;\n  flagReview(reviewId: number): void;\n  getFlaggedReviews(): Review[];\n  removeReview(reviewId: number): boolean;\n  getReviewsByUser(userId: string): Review[];\n  getReviewCount(pluginName: string): number;\n\nReview = { id: number; pluginName: string; pluginVersion: string; userId: string; rating: number; comment: string; flagged: boolean; createdAt: string }\n\nRequirements:\n- import Database from 'better-sqlite3';\n- In the factory, create: const db = new Database(':memory:'); and CREATE TABLE reviews with columns: id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, pluginName TEXT, pluginVersion TEXT, userId TEXT, rating INTEGER, comment TEXT, flagged INTEGER DEFAULT 0, createdAt TEXT.\n- addReview: insert with flagged=0 and createdAt = new Date().toISOString(); return the full Review row (with the generated id, flagged:false). Convert the integer 'flagged' column to a boolean in all returned Review objects.\n- getReviews(pluginName): all reviews for that plugin (include flagged ones).\n- getAverageRating(pluginName): average rating EXCLUDING flagged reviews; return 0 if there are no non-flagged reviews.\n- flagReview(reviewId): set flagged=1 for that id.\n- getFlaggedReviews(): all reviews where flagged=1.\n- removeReview(reviewId): delete; return true if a row was deleted (use the run() result's .changes), false otherwise.\n- getReviewsByUser(userId): all reviews by that user.\n- getReviewCount(pluginName): total number of reviews for that plugin (count all, including flagged).\n- Write a small private helper to map a DB row to a Review (converting flagged 0/1 -> boolean). Type DB rows carefully WITHOUT using 'any' (define a row interface or use 'unknown' + narrowing; better-sqlite3 .get()/.all() can be typed via generics e.g. stmt.all(x) as RowType[]).\n`)\n\nconst DEPS = shared(`\nTASK: Create file src/deps/index.ts implementing the Dependency Graph analyzer.\n\nExport a factory: export function createDeps(): DepsService\n\nDepsService interface:\n  buildTree(name: string, registry: RegistryService): DependencyNode;\n  detectCycles(name: string, registry: RegistryService): string[][] | null;\n  topologicalSort(name: string, registry: RegistryService): string[];\n  flattenDependencies(name: string, registry: RegistryService): string[];\n  hasCircularDependency(name: string, registry: RegistryService): boolean;\n\nDependencyNode = { name: string; version: string; dependencies: DependencyNode[] }\nRegistryService has: get(name): PluginManifest | null  (latest version), and manifest.dependencies is Record<string, string> (depName -> semver range).\n\nRequirements (you only import type { DependencyNode, RegistryService, PluginManifest } from '../types.js'):\n- Resolve each plugin via registry.get(name) to obtain its manifest (use manifest.version for the node's version, and Object.keys(manifest.dependencies) for child names). If registry.get(name) returns null, treat the node as having version 'unknown'/'' and no dependencies (a missing/leaf node) — do NOT throw.\n- buildTree(name, registry): build a DependencyNode tree by recursively expanding dependencies. To avoid infinite recursion on cycles, track the current ancestor path; if a name is already in the current path, stop expanding it (treat it as a leaf with empty dependencies) rather than recursing forever.\n- detectCycles(name, registry): perform DFS tracking the current path; whenever you reach a node already on the current path, record the cycle as the array of names from the first occurrence of that node to the repeated node (e.g. ['a','b','a']). Return an array of such cycle paths. Return null if NO cycles exist. De-duplicate cycles if practical.\n- hasCircularDependency(name, registry): return true iff detectCycles(...) is non-null and non-empty.\n- topologicalSort(name, registry): return a topological ordering of all plugin names reachable from 'name' (including 'name'), such that dependencies come BEFORE the plugins that depend on them. If there is a cycle, do not infinite-loop — produce a best-effort ordering (e.g. via DFS post-order with a visited set). Each name appears once.\n- flattenDependencies(name, registry): return the unique list of all TRANSITIVE dependency names reachable from 'name', EXCLUDING 'name' itself. Order is not critical but must be cycle-safe (use a visited set).\n- Be careful with 'any': type everything; use Record/Set<string>/string[] etc.\n`)\n\nconst results = await parallel([\n  () => agent(REGISTRY, { label: 'registry', phase: 'Build modules' }),\n  () => agent(RESOLVER, { label: 'resolver', phase: 'Build modules' }),\n  () => agent(RUNNER, { label: 'runner', phase: 'Build modules' }),\n  () => agent(REVIEWS, { label: 'reviews', phase: 'Build modules' }),\n  () => agent(DEPS, { label: 'deps', phase: 'Build modules' }),\n])\n\nreturn {\n  registry: results[0],\n  resolver: results[1],\n  runner: results[2],\n  reviews: results[3],\n  deps: results[4],\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2102,"cache_read_input_tokens":28761,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2102},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c92c4f0-a47c-4dc1-9889-e1b15fdbf985","uuid":"abc35330-8f2b-4f49-b61b-4eaa5b636dd6","request_id":"req_011CbVZdCU99VP8T6NR9veCr"}
